[user-comment] Title: Long OpenGL sessions crash when the 48 x 1 GB jumbo reservation cap fills (only 10 MB committed); swap never engages (Mewgenics, 0xc0000005)  Summary Mewgenics ran for about 46 minutes, then crashed with 0xc0000005 as a new area loaded. BCD refused a 1 GB address-space reservation because it already held 48 big reservations with almost nothing committed. The game doesn't check for the failure and wrote through a null pointer. I think this is an allocator problem in BCD, not a game bug or a real out-of-memory.  Why this likely affects other games The failure is in BCD's generic big-reservation allocator, not anything specific to Mewgenics. Any OpenGL game that keeps requesting 1 GB reservations in a long session could fill the same cap and crash the same way. I've only tested Mewgenics, so I can't confirm other games.  Environment - iPad (M3 GPU), BCD build 634, JIT via debugger, iPadOS idiom=pad - Mewgenics (Steam app 686060) launched through BCD Dock - api=OpenGL/64, 1920x1080, thermal=serious at start - Settings: swap-mb=2048, MADEIRA_FPS_CAP=60, increased-memory-limit=true, extended-virtual-addressing=false - Session summary: length=2771s play=2750s avg=42.8fps peak=7682MB limit=8191MB  Repro 1. Launch Mewgenics through BCD, play normally for about 45 minutes. 2. Enter a boss fight. 3. The game exits with 0xc0000005. I haven't tried to reproduce it a second time.  Evidence (log: Mewgenics.exe-2026-11-07_03-58-25.txt) - [jumbo#268] size=0x40000000 (1024 MB) -> 0x0 st=0xc0000017 | granted=273408 MB ok=267 fail=1 - [va-owners] jumbo reserve failed: 48 big reservation(s) held by 1 owner(s) - [bigres-use] ranges=48 reserved=49152 MB committed=10 MB (0%) touched=48/48 (jumbo fail) - [nt-fail] NtAllocateVirtualMemory status=c0000017 size=0x40000000 type=0x2000 (MEM_RESERVE) - Crash: AV WRITE of 8 at Mewgenics.exe+0x969604, x0=0x0 (null pointer + 8, using the result of the failed allocation) - [dock-game-end] mewgenics.exe ended with status 0xc00000
